1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,352
Off one Sri Lankan beach,

2
00:00:02,352 --> 00:00:04,745
the largest animal that has ever

3
00:00:04,745 --> 00:00:07,264
lived swims just a short boat ride

4
00:00:07,264 --> 00:00:08,934
from shore.

5
00:00:09,884 --> 00:00:11,722
Why here? Off Mirissa,

6
00:00:11,722 --> 00:00:13,889
the seabed drops away fast.

7
00:00:13,889 --> 00:00:16,449
The edge of the continental shelf

8
00:00:16,449 --> 00:00:19,347
lies only 7–8 kilometres out.

9
00:00:20,297 --> 00:00:21,843
Along the steep slope,

10
00:00:21,843 --> 00:00:23,279
deep water wells up,

11
00:00:23,279 --> 00:00:25,488
carrying nutrients to the surface.

12
00:00:25,488 --> 00:00:26,702
Plankton blooms,

13
00:00:26,702 --> 00:00:28,580
and tiny shrimp-like animals

14
00:00:28,580 --> 00:00:30,450
gather in swarms.

15
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:33,017
These are blue whales

16
00:00:33,017 --> 00:00:35,113
of the northern Indian Ocean.

17
00:00:35,113 --> 00:00:36,910
Unlike most blue whales,

18
00:00:36,910 --> 00:00:39,185
they don't migrate to cold polar

19
00:00:39,185 --> 00:00:41,102
seas, and some stay around

20
00:00:41,102 --> 00:00:43,199
Sri Lanka all year.

21
00:00:44,149 --> 00:00:45,792
From November to April,

22
00:00:45,792 --> 00:00:47,322
when the sea is calm,

23
00:00:47,322 --> 00:00:49,192
boats leave Mirissa harbour

24
00:00:49,192 --> 00:00:50,268
to find them,

25
00:00:50,268 --> 00:00:51,911
along with sperm whales

26
00:00:51,911 --> 00:00:53,588
and dolphins.

27
00:00:55,388 --> 00:00:57,127
But the same waters carry

28
00:00:57,127 --> 00:00:58,922
one of the world's busiest

29
00:00:58,922 --> 00:01:01,054
shipping lanes. Ship strikes are

30
00:01:01,054 --> 00:01:03,130
the biggest threat these whales

31
00:01:03,130 --> 00:01:04,347
face.

32
00:01:05,297 --> 00:01:07,998
Scientists estimate that moving

33
00:01:07,998 --> 00:01:10,773
the lane 15 nautical miles south

34
00:01:10,773 --> 00:01:12,525
could cut the risk

35
00:01:12,525 --> 00:01:15,153
by about 95 per cent. In 2022,

36
00:01:15,153 --> 00:01:17,563
the shipping line MSC moved

37
00:01:17,563 --> 00:01:19,331
its route.

38
00:01:20,281 --> 00:01:23,108
By law, boats must stay at least

39
00:01:23,108 --> 00:01:25,860
100 metres away, and no one may

40
00:01:25,860 --> 00:01:28,687
swim with them without a special

41
00:01:28,687 --> 00:01:30,254
permit.

42
00:01:31,204 --> 00:01:32,501
Give them space,

43
00:01:32,501 --> 00:01:34,622
and the giants of Mirissa stay

44
00:01:34,622 --> 00:01:36,460
close to shore.
